## Findings

- **N1 — high** at [delegate.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2823723771/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1126): cancel does not resume release once the failed run is recorded but its receipt is still missing, so dispatch stays blocked.
- **N2 — medium** at [delegation_release.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2823723771/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:100): takeover of a dead release claim is a non-atomic compare-and-replace, so concurrent cancels can both record release runs.
- **N3 — medium** at [delegation_release.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2823723771/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:177): recovery ignores run-history read losses and can treat an unreadable prior run as absent.

R3-N1 is partial; R3-N2 and R3-N3 are fixed. The whole round‑4 change was swept.

Focused tests and `go vet` passed. Both strict validation reruns were blocked before checks because the read-only sandbox could not create Go build directories; the draft cites sealed build and unit evidence. The checkout remained clean.

